    {
      "id": "claim_5e8a2f6f04f346aa8fc13c468aef5726",
      "statement": "executor.Executor.Execute distinguishes three failure situations that all currently map to the same terminal RunResult status \"failed\" in the worker but are logically distinct: a target-derivation error before authorization ran (Result.Error set, Allowed false by zero value, not treated as a denial), an explicit authorization denial (Allowed false, Reason set, Error nil), and a successful-authorization-but-failed Scope.Run (Allowed true, Error set).",
